  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer array numsnumsnums, find the **subarray** with the largest sum, and print its sum.\n\n**Note**: A subarray is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT, the number of test cases.\nThe first line in each test case contains NNN, the number of elements in an array.\nThe second line in each test case contains NNN integers, denoting the elements in the array.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum subarray sum of each array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 100",
      "1 <= N <= 100",
      "-10^9 <= Ai <= 10^9"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. For each test case, the first line contains an integer N, the number of elements in the array. The second line contains N space‑separated integers denoting the array.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, output a single line containing the maximum possible sum of any non‑empty contiguous subarray.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n9\n-2 1 -3 4 -1 2 1 -5 4\n1\n1\n5\n5 4 -1 7 8",
        "output": "6\n1\n23",
        "explanation": "First array: maximum subarray is [4, -1, 2, 1] with sum 6. Second array: only element 1, sum 1. Third array: all elements sum to 23, which is the maximum."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n-1 -2 -3 -4\n3\n1 2 3",
        "output": "-1\n6",
        "explanation": "All numbers are negative, so the best subarray is the largest single element -1. All numbers are positive, so the whole array sum 6 is maximal."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n5\n-1 2 3 -4 5",
        "output": "6",
        "explanation": "Kadane's algorithm yields a maximum sum of 6 from subarray [2, 3, -4, 5]."
      }
    ]
  },
