  "solution": {
    "approach": "The problem asks for the maximum sum over all contiguous subarrays. The optimal solution is Kadane's algorithm, which scans the array while maintaining the best subarray ending at the current position. For each element x we update current = max(x, current + x) – either we start a new subarray at x or extend the previous one. The global answer is the maximum of all current values. This runs in linear time and uses O(1) extra space, satisfying the constraints.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(N) per test case, O(total N) over all test cases.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) – only a few variables are used irrespective of N.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;import java.util.*;public class Main{public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception{BufferedReader br=new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();int T=Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());for(int t=0;t<T;++t){int N=Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());StringTokenizer st=new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());long x=Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());long cur=x,best=x;for(int i=1;i<N;++i){x=Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());cur=Math.max(x,cur+x);best=Math.max(best,cur);}sb.append(best);if(t<T-1) sb.append('\\n');}System.out.print(sb.toString());}}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
